1
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:09,333
The much loved Australian story of an outback family and a
Christmas adventure that they would never forget.

2
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:12,666
Bush Christmas is a family, adventure, drama film directed by Henri Safran.

3
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
In the Australian outback a family struggles to keep its farm from foreclosure.

4
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:19,333
Their only hope is that their horse, Prince, will
win money in a New Year's race.

5
00:25:16,666 --> 00:25:22,666
But when Prince is stolen the children embark on a
dangerous and exciting adventure to get him back.

6
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Bill, played by John Ewart.

7
00:35:23,333 --> 00:35:29,333
Sly, played by John Howard.

8
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
John Thompson, played by Mark Spain.

9
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Helen, played by Nicole Kidman.

10
00:50:33,333 --> 00:50:39,333
Ben Thompson, played by Peter Sumner.

11
00:55:36,666 --> 00:55:42,666
Manalpuy, played by Manalpuy.

12
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Bush Christmas (also known as Prince and the Great Race) is a 1983 Australian
Christmas drama film and a remake of the 1947 film of the same name.

13
01:05:43,333 --> 01:05:49,333
The film marked actress Nicole Kidman's first feature film role.

14
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
It was filmed on location on the Lamington Plateau, Queensland.

15
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
It is also notable for music by the Bushwackers.

16
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The film explores themes of horse race, money problems,
rustlers, christmas, australian bush.

17
01:25:56,666 --> 01:26:02,666
The tone is emotional.
